<title>USA: Harley-Davidson settles $9.9 mln lawsuit.</title>
<headline>Harley-Davidson settles $9.9 mln lawsuit.</headline>
<dateline>MILWAUKEE 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Harley-Davidson Inc on Monday said a judge in a New Jersey superior court vacated a $9.9 million judgment in a product liability lawsuit filed after a 1991 motorcycle accident.</p>
<p>Harley said the matter has been completely resolved by settlement, although further details were not released.</p>
<p>In February, a jury awarded the plaintiff, Thomas Molinaro of Pen Argyl, Pennsylvania, $9.9 million in compensatory damages after an accident that resulted in severe pelvic injuries and Molinaro's right leg being amputated.</p>
<p>Molinaro's attorney had said a device that acted like a cruise control on Molinaro's 1987 Harley motorcycle did not disengage as he went around a curve on a road in New Jersey.</p>
<p>Harley shares closed down 3/8 at 37.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
